    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n60 Palmerston Road is a distinguished Victorian residence of wonderful character and elegance, occupying a lovely position on one of Dublin's most prestigious and sought-after residential roads. Ideally located between Ormond Road and Windsor Road, the property is within a short stroll of both Beechwood and Cowper Luas stops, offering superb convenience in the heart of Dublin 6.\nExtending to approximately 274 sq.m. (2,949 sq.ft.), this impressive light-filled home has been sensitively refurbished and modernised over the years. A wealth of original period features, including ornate ceiling plasterwork, fine mantelpieces and sash windows, combine seamlessly with a timeless contemporary aesthetic to create a home perfectly suited to modern family living.\nGranite steps lead to an elegant entrance hall, setting the tone for the accommodation within. At hall level, two gracious interconnecting reception rooms provide superb spaces for both entertaining and everyday family life. Upstairs, there are three generous double bedrooms with the principal suite enjoying delightful views over Palmerston Road and benefiting from an adjoining dressing room and contemporary en suite shower room.\nAt garden level, the beautifully designed open-plan kitchen flows effortlessly into a spacious family room and dining area, creating a superb living space and the true heart of the home.\nThe private rear garden is designed for ease of maintenance and is bordered by fencing and shrubs, providing a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion. To the front, the landscaped garden incorporates a generous, gravelled parking area framed by mature hedging and shrubbery. Hidden behind the hedging lies a sizeable, paved terrace perfect for a quiet morning coffee.\nThe location is second to none. Rathmines, Rathgar and Ranelagh villages are all within easy walking distance and offer an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and local amenities. Local shopping at Upper Rathmines Road and Dunville Avenue are a true local treasure. Recreational facilities nearby include David Lloyd Riverview, Fitzwilliam Lawn Tennis Club, Brookfield Tennis Club and Dartry Health Club. The area is also renowned for its exceptional choice of schools, including Scoil Bhríde, Kildare Place School, Alexandra College, St Mary's College, Muckross Park, Sandford Park and Gonzaga College.\nCombining elegant Victorian architecture with contemporary comfort and style, not to mention much sought-after off-street parking, 60 Palmerston Road is a truly special family home which presents a great opportunity to acquire a substantial period residence in one of Dublin 6's most desirable addresses."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nOriginal hall door with skylight, limestone floor, cornice, centre rose and archway, antique style radiator\n\nDrawing Room - \nTall sash window with working shutters, cornice, picture rail and centre rose, marble mantlepiece with tiled hearth & fitted with gas fire, folding doors to:\n\nDining Room - \nLarge sash window overlooking rear garden, matching marble mantlepiece with tiled hearth and fitted with gas fire\n\nHall Return - \n\n\nBathroom - \nWC, wash hand basin on vanity unit, bath with stone surround and mixer tap, two windows with opaque glass, tiled floor, recessed lights\n\nGarden Level - \nSide entrance to hallway, understairs storage plumbed for washing machine and dryer, door to:\n\nInner Hallway - \nPorcelain tiled floor, archway, large opening to\n\nKitchen - \nHandmade painted kitchen with large range of floor and wall units incorporating Belfast sink, Aga (runs off gas), Siemens gas hob, full height integrated fridge, stone countertop. Large island with matching stone countertop incorporating Electrolux oven, Candy microwave, Bosch dishwasher, bin store, Hoover wine cooler. Large display cabinet with extensive storage. Tiled floor, recessed lights, double door to rear garden\n\nDining area - \nTiled floor continues, picture window and double doors to rear garden, recessed lights, door to hallway\n\nFamily Room - \nSolid wood floor, sash window overlooking front garden, large open fireplace fitted with gas stove, recessed lights\n\nFirst Floor - \nLanding with skylight, recessed light\n\nBedroom 1 front - \nLarge double with sash windows, open fireplace with painted mantlepiece and tiled surround, coving, opening to:\n\nWalk-in wardrobe - \nWith large range of floor to ceiling fitted wardrobes, opening to\n\nEnsuite Shower Room - \nWC, wash hand basin on vanity unit, shower cubicle with rainwater shower head and hand attachment, heated radiator, recessed lights, window with opaque glass\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble room with sash window, fitted wardrobe, open fireplace with painted mantlepiece and tiled surround, dado rail and coving\n\nBedroom 3 - \nDouble to rear, cornice, fitted wardrobe\n\nSecond Floor Return - \n\n\nShower Room - \nWC, wash hand basin, shower cubicle with wall mounted shower, tiled floor, part tiled walls, small window, recessed lights\n\nRear garden - \nWalled and fenced private garden bordered with hedging and laid out with paving and shrubbery, garden shed. Ideal for al fresco dining.\n\nFront garden - \nRailed garden bordered with hedging and shrubbery, vehicular and pedestrian entrance, gravelled with parking for two cars, private patio area, railed granite steps to hall door\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Handsome two-storey over garden level terraced Victorian home</li><li>Well-appointed accommodation of 274 sqm / 2949 sqft approx.</li><li>3 bedrooms (1 ensuite), 3 reception rooms & 2 bathrooms</li><li>Beautiful original period features</li><li>Secure off-street parking for 2 vehicles</li><li>Private, low maintenance rear garden </li><li>Superbly located on Palmerston Road</li><li>Close to Beechwood and Cowper Luas stops, local shopping at Dunville Avenue, Ranelagh and Rathmines</ul>"
      },
